# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
RAILWAY SAFETY FUSION  -  TF-Luna LiDAR + HC-SR04 ultrasonic + Pi camera + 16x2 I2C LCD
Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (2 GB), Raspberry Pi OS Bookworm / Trixie

INSTALL (once)
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install -y python3-picamera2 python3-opencv python3-numpy python3-serial \
                        python3-smbus2 python3-pip i2c-tools
    pip3 install RPLCD --break-system-packages
    # RPi.GPIO is normally preinstalled. If "import RPi.GPIO" fails:  sudo apt install -y python3-rpi-lgpio
    sudo raspi-config nonint do_i2c 0           # enable I2C
    sudo raspi-config nonint do_serial_cons 1   # serial login shell OFF
    sudo raspi-config nonint do_serial_hw 0     # serial hardware ON
    sudo reboot

RUN
    python3 railway_safety_fusion.py                 # with preview window
    python3 railway_safety_fusion.py --headless      # no monitor (SSH)
    keys in the window:  q / Esc = quit,  r = relearn background,  m = show/hide mask
    headless:            kill -USR1 <pid> = relearn background

WIRING (BCM)
    TF-Luna   TX -> GPIO15 (RXD, Pin 10)   RX -> GPIO14 (TXD, Pin 8)   5V / GND      (/dev/serial0, 115200)
    HC-SR04   TRIG -> GPIO23 (Pin 16)      ECHO -> GPIO24 (Pin 18) through a 1k + 2k voltage divider
    LCD I2C   SDA -> GPIO2 (Pin 3)         SCL -> GPIO3 (Pin 5)    5V / GND          (0x27, falls back to 0x3F)
    Camera    CSI ribbon cable

DECISION MATRIX
    CRITICAL STOP       lidar < 40 cm  OR  ultrasonic < 40 cm  OR  large obstacle in camera CENTER zone
    CAUTION: SIDE OBST  both ranges >= 40 cm BUT an obstacle is seen in the camera LEFT or RIGHT zone
    CLEAR               nothing detected anywhere

NOTE  Do not run this at the same time as the dashboard (railwayproject2.py / railway.service): both want the
      camera, the serial port, the GPIO pins and the LCD.  Stop it first:  sudo systemctl stop railway.service
"""
